<title>USA: TABLE - CBT Corp Q2 shr flat.</title>
<headline>TABLE - CBT Corp Q2 shr flat.</headline>
<dateline>PADUCAH, Ky. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>($ in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>					  June 30,	     June 30,</p>
<p>					1997     1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Total assets (a)	    993,963  916,950  993,963  916,950</p>
<p> Net income			3,202    3,198    6,333    6,130</p>
<p> Earnings per share	     0.41     0.41     0.81     0.78</p>
<p> Dividends declared	     0.13     0.12     0.26     0.24</p>
<p> Market value - high	   24.50    24.25    26.50    24.50</p>
<p> Market value - low	    20.25    21.50    20.25    21.50</p>
<p> Book value per share (a)    14.56    13.37    14.56    13.37</p>
<p> Net interest margin (t/e)   4.81%    5.05%    4.81%    5.01%</p>
<p> Efficiency ratio (t/e)	56.57    58.76    56.66    59.76</p>
<p>Return on average assets (b)</p>
<p>					1.31     1.41     1.32     1.36</p>
<p>Return on average equity (b)</p>
<p>				     11.23    12.00    11.29    11.61</p>
<p>Ending equity to total assets (a)</p>
<p>				     11.52    11.47    11.52    11.47</p>
<p>NOTES: Q2 1997 earnings were enhanced by gains on sale of securities ($56,000 pre-tax) and finance receivables ($148,000 pre-tax). The after-tax impact of these asset sales, which were accomplished to redeploy resources within the corporation, was $122,000 ($0.16 per share).</p>
<p>Year-to-date, asset sales have netted an after-tax gain of $222,000 ($.028 per share).</p>
<p>(a) Includes SFAS 115</p>
<p>(b) Excludes SFAS 115</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
